5,Wakhi language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Wakhi_language,"January 21, 2026 - The Wakhi language belongs to the Eastern Iranian branch of the Indo-Iranian languages within the Indo-European family.[4][7] It is spoken by approximately 72,000 people across Central Asia, primarily in the Pamir Mountains.[4] Within Eastern Iranian languages, Wakhi is classified as a member of the Southeastern subgroup, specifically among the Pamir languages, which include Shughni-Yazghulami, Ishkashimi-Sanglechi, and others.[8] This affiliation is supported by shared phonological, morphological, and lexical features, such as the retention of certain proto-Iranian sounds and ergative-absolut",Wakhi,Indo-European
